  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 17A—Protected international trade marks under the Madrid Protocol",
    "Division 3—International registration designating Australia",
    "Subdivision 1—General",
    "17A.17  Examination—holder’s response to report"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "17A.17",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r17A.17",
  "text": "(1) The holder of the IRDA may respond in writing to the Registrar’s report under regulation 17A.16. (2) The response may do any of the following: (a) contest a belief of the Registrar that is expressed in the report; (b) contest another matter that is mentioned in the report; (c) provide further documents or evidence in support of the IRDA; (d) request a hearing from the Registrar. (3) The holder must notify the Registrar, in writing, of the holder’s address for service in Australia or New Zealand.",
